      "content": "The \"random error\" you're referring to is often addressed through the concept of sampling variability, which is what your confidence interval is designed to capture. To sound professional, you can discuss the *precision* of your estimate rather than just the error itself. You might mention that the confidence interval reflects the range within which the true population parameter is likely to fall, given the sample size. If you have specific outliers, you should report them descriptively, perhaps noting their presence but explaining how robust your main findings are against their influence.",
